{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.StarOrdered","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRealUniqueness","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalKnotIdSDPUniqueness"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_uniqueness_closed_via_active_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_uniqueness_closed_via_active_empty","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L267-L283","doc":"**Sorry-free, axiom-free uniqueness via the active-empty route.**\nDischarged by\n`real_strict_complementarity_unique_of_active_empty_and_cost_posDef`\n(active set empty + identity cost PosDef).  Complements\n`nucleus_uniqueness_closed` (dual-slack-PosDef route) with the\nargument whose hypotheses match the R5-full witness's `active = ∅`\nfinding directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusTrivialRealStrictCompPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusTrivialRealStrictCompPair","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L257-L265","doc":"**Trivial real strict-complementarity pair** for the empty SDP:\nempty active set, optimum `Φ⋆ = 0`.  (`ι = Empty`, so the\nactive/inactive dual obligations are discharged by `Empty.elim`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_objAt_optimum_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_objAt_optimum_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L235-L239","doc":"The objective value at the (zero) optimum is exactly 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_optimum_is_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_optimum_is_zero","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L230-L233","doc":"The optimum Φ⋆ is the zero matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_uniqueness_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_uniqueness_closed","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L215-L228","doc":"**Sorry-free uniqueness for the generic empty SDP** — via the\ninterior-case closure of the strict-complementarity uniqueness\ntheorem. No `sorry` in the chain\n`nucleusRealStrongDualityPair → nucleus_dualSlack_posDef →\nreal_strict_complementarity_unique_of_dualSlack_posDef`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_dualSlack_posDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_dualSlack_posDef","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L204-L213","doc":"**Dual slack is PosDef** for the generic empty SDP. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusRealStrongDualityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusRealStrongDualityPair","kind":"def","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L188-L202","doc":"**Real strong-duality pair** for the generic empty SDP. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusEmptySDP_Φstar_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusEmptySDP_Φstar_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L169-L172","doc":"**Trivial Φ⋆ is the zero matrix** (by construction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_uniqueness_via_empty_sdp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleus_uniqueness_via_empty_sdp","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L148-L167","doc":"**Generic Subsingleton uniqueness via the abstract bridge.**\nUnder the trivial strict-complementarity pair for the\nempty-constraint SDP, the primal optimum is unique among\nfeasible matrices achieving the same objective.\n\nNow routed through the **proven interior-case** closure\n(`real_strict_complementarity_unique_of_dualSlack_posDef`): the\nempty-constraint SDP has `cost = 1` and no constraints, so its dual\nslack is the identity, which is positive-definite.\n\nIt used to depend on `strict_complementarity_unique_axiom`, which was\n**false** and has been deleted (bean `qou-i6u4`).  The statement is\nunchanged and still true — only the route was rotten. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusTrivialStrictCompPair_dualSlack_posDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusTrivialStrictCompPair_dualSlack_posDef","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L137-L146","doc":"The dual slack at the trivial pair is the identity, hence PosDef. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusTrivialStrictCompPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusTrivialStrictCompPair","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L108-L135","doc":"**Trivial strict-complementarity pair for the generic empty\nSDP.** Active set is empty; the optimum is at `Φ⋆ = 0`.\n\nThis is a `RealStrictComplementarityPair`, not the generic\n`StrictComplementarityPair` of `SDPEmptyConstraints`: the generic\nstructure's `dual_feas` and `obj_eq` fields are `True` placeholders,\nso it carries no duality content, and the generic uniqueness route\nover it was deleted as false (bean `qou-i6u4`).  The real pair below\ndischarges genuine `dualSlack_psd` and `obj_eq_dualObj` obligations\nand feeds the proven interior-case closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusEmptySDP_strictlyFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusEmptySDP_strictlyFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L101-L106","doc":"The empty-constraint SDP at `heckeDim n` is strictly feasible\n(identity matrix is positive-definite, no constraints to\nviolate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusEmptySDP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nucleusEmptySDP","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/NucleusEmptySDPUniqueness.lean#L92-L99","doc":"**Generic empty-constraint SDP at Hecke dimension `heckeDim n`.**\nCost matrix is the identity; no equality constraints\n(`ι := Empty`). Parameter `n` is the nucleus's strand count\n`3A` where `A = Z + N`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}